# Telegram notify — every result / error / status

After **every** meaningful work landing (success, failure, blocker, or status change) in this conversation, send a short Telegram summary immediately.

## How

Run from repo root (or absolute path):

```bash
bash scripts/telegram-notify.sh <kind> "<short summary>"
```

- `kind`: `result` | `error` | `status`
- Summary: 1–5 short lines, no secrets, no full logs
- Script reads `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` from env (same as n8n `$env['TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN']`) and `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` (default `217250285`) from env or `.telegram-config`

## When (mandatory)

- Build/install OK or FAIL
- Pack apply OK or FAIL
- Missing credentials / blocked waiting on user
- Task finished with a deliverable or an error
- Any status the user cannot see in chat (Mac worker idle/busy, log missing, etc.)

## Do not

- Skip notify because chat already has text
- Put bot token or other secrets in the message
- Ask the user to paste the token into chat
